"causes":["Kinetic strike"],"members":[{"date":"2026-03-02","date_precision":"day","region":"National","effect":null,"withheld":true}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"sa","country":"Saudi Arabia","episode_id":"sa-row-11","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2026-02-23","last_date":"2026-02-23","date_precision":"day","classes":["Gas processing"],"causes":["Unknown"],"members":[{"date":"2026-02-23","date_precision":"day","region":"National","effect":null,"withheld":true}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"iq","country":"Iraq","episode_id":"iq-row-12","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2025-12-23","last_date":"2025-12-23","date_precision":"day","classes":["System-wide (grid area or supply system)"],"causes":["Unknown"],"members":[{"date":"2025-12-23","date_precision":"day","region":"National","effect":"Ministry of Electricity, as carried by Attaqa: between 4,000 and 4,500 MW of generation lost; some units stopped and others load-limited; reduced supply hours in a number of governorates (not named). The ministry said it was running affected stations on domestic fuel.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"iq","country":"Iraq","episode_id":"iq-row-13","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2025-12-08","last_date":"2025-12-08","date_precision":"day","classes":["Upstream production"],"causes":["Technical accident"],"members":[{"date":"2025-12-08","date_precision":"day","region":"Al-Basrah","effect":"Two sources, one at the oil ministry and one at Basra Oil Company, told Rudaw that production at the field, which was producing roughly 480,000 barrels a day, was halted (Rudaw, 8 December 2025); Attaqa reported the same halt and volume the same day and said the ministry did not answer a request for comment.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"iq","country":"Iraq","episode_id":"iq-row-14","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2025-08-11","last_date":"2025-08-11","date_precision":"day","classes":["System-wide (grid area or supply system)"],"causes":["Technical accident"],"members":[{"date":"2025-08-11","date_precision":"day","region":"Multiple regions","effect":"Ministry of Electricity, as carried by Asharq News and Arabi21: the grid lost more than 6,000 MW suddenly and accidentally, leading to a complete blackout; the ministry said it was working under full emergency footing. Media and local sources reported loss of power in Basra, Maysan, Dhi Qar, Wasit, Baghdad, Diyala, Anbar and Kirkuk.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"kw","country":"Kuwait","episode_id":"kw-row-15","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2025-04-09","last_date":"2025-04-10","date_precision":"day","classes":["System-wide (grid area or supply system)"],"causes":["Unknown"],"members":[{"date":"2025-04-09","date_precision":"day","region":"Multiple regions","effect":"The electricity ministry stated on 13 April 2025 that loads on 9 and 10 April 2025 were about 21% and 17.3% above the same period of the previous year, 'which required implementing a programme of programmed cuts'. The press reported that on 9 April the ministry cut power to parts of some residential, agricultural and industrial areas, eight residential areas being named, under what the ministry called an emergency plan for peak loads.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"kw","country":"Kuwait","episode_id":"kw-row-16","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2024-09-10","last_date":"2024-09-10","date_precision":"day","classes":["System-wide (grid area or supply system)"],"causes":["Technical accident"],"members":[{"date":"2024-09-10","date_precision":"day","region":"Multiple regions","effect":"The electricity ministry announced on 10 September 2024 that it was cutting power to parts of 11 residential areas; the press reported an emergency outage of two generating units, 390 MW together according to an unnamed ministry source.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"kw","country":"Kuwait","episode_id":"kw-row-17","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2024-08-18","last_date":"2024-08-19","date_precision":"day","classes":["System-wide (grid area or supply system)"],"causes":["Unknown"],"members":[{"date":"2024-08-18","date_precision":"day","region":"Multiple regions","effect":"The electricity ministry, in a statement carried by the state news agency on 18 August 2024, attributed the cuts to 'a fault in fuel (gas) supplies' that took generating units out of service, and said the cuts were made to keep the grid stable. On 19 August the ministry said cuts in nine agricultural and industrial areas were applied in turn because of the gas supply problem.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"kw","country":"Kuwait","episode_id":"kw-row-18","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2024-06-19","last_date":"2024-06-20","date_precision":"day","classes":["System-wide (grid area or supply system)"],"causes":["Unknown"],"members":[{"date":"2024-06-19","date_precision":"day","region":"Multiple regions","effect":"The electricity ministry stated on 19 June 2024 that the cuts in parts of the six governorates were due to 'the inability of the power generating plants to meet the rising demand during the peak period', applied as programmed cuts of one to two hours at most. The press counted about 40 areas and reported a 300 MW generating unit out of service that day.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"om","country":"Oman","episode_id":"om-row-19","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2022-09-05","last_date":"2022-09-06","date_precision":"day","classes":["System-wide (grid area or supply system)"],"causes":["Technical accident"],"members":[{"date":"2022-09-05","date_precision":"day","region":"Multiple regions","effect":"Power was lost from early afternoon. The Authority for Public Services Regulation confirmed a partial blackout across Muscat and parts of four other governorates (The National and Al Bayan, 5 September 2022, both carrying the regulator's statement). Oman Observer reported commercial and industrial activity disrupted for between six and twelve hours and, citing the regulator's data, described the outage as the \"most serious in a decade\". Schools in affected areas were closed the next day.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0},{"system_id":"sa","country":"Saudi Arabia","episode_id":"sa-row-20","episode_name":null,"basis":"singleton","records":1,"first_date":"2022-03-20","last_date":"2022-03-20","date_precision":"day","classes":["Oil refinery"],"causes":["Kinetic strike"],"members":[{"date":"2022-03-20","date_precision":"day","region":"Al Madinah","effect":"Ministry: the attack led to a temporary reduction in the refinery's production. No volume or duration given.","withheld":false}],"more_members":0}]}}